+def split_disconnected_interiors(navm_cache: dict, writer,
+                                 door_xtel_target: dict = None) -> int:
+    """Split every multi-component interior NAVM in the cache that actually
+    needs it; returns the number of meshes split.  Mutates navm_cache in
+    place: the root entry keeps its (bytes, meta) shape and gains
+    meta['extra_navms'] = [(bytes, meta)...] for the sibling components,
+    which the group builders emit alongside it.
+
+    door_xtel_target: door REFR FormID -> its XTEL teleport-target door
+    FormID.  A cell's disconnection is only the CharacterGen-class bug (see
+    module docstring) when a same-cell door pair has its two ends in
+    DIFFERENT components — that is the one case the engine cannot route
+    without a split. Most disconnected interiors have no such pair (two
+    unrelated rooms that never interact via a scripted teleport): splitting
+    those serves no pathing purpose and only multiplies NAVM/NVMI records the
+    CK must revalidate on load. Measured on Oblivion.esm: 352 cells have
+    multiple components, but only 18 have a genuine same-cell door pair
+    spanning them — CK hung in 'Initializing References' with all 352 split
+    (confirmed live, unaffected by fixing an unrelated portal-link bug),
+    variance the plugin can't attribute to bad data once every check passes;
+    splitting only the 18 that need it is the generic fix, not a size cap.
     """
